{"version":1,"pending":[{"id":"cb415b30-3659-47d6-aa6f-226f0f4d61a8","secret":"","createdAt":"2026-11-05T22:21:09.835Z"},{"id":"0b7dbc2e-c678-4591-8e38-0a5efd42b27f","secret":"","createdAt":"2026-11-05T22:18:30.898Z"}],"published":[{"id":"8c7d6a1b-71b3-4228-bfb8-5ac5eca7fe10","authorId":"d60cf04a2b460077a855f5a431c2","publicByline":"Carlos Aleman Jr","identity":"real","title":"The Light in the Window","body":"Every evening, a little girl watched her father turn on the porch light.\n\n\"Why do you leave it on all night?\" she asked.\n\nHer father smiled.\n\n\"So anyone trying to find their way home can see where they're going.\"\n\nYears passed, and the little girl grew older.\n\nEventually, she moved away and experienced the difficulties of adulthood.\n\nThere were moments when life felt overwhelming and she wondered whether she had lost her way.\n\nOne evening, after a particularly difficult day, she returned to her childhood home.\n\nAs she turned onto the familiar street, she noticed something.\n\nThe porch light was still shining.\n\nHer father was waiting at the door.\n\nShe realized that the light had never been about electricity.\n\nIt was about love.\n\nIt was about hope.\n\nIt was about knowing that no matter how dark the journey became, there was still somewhere she belonged.\n\nAnd perhaps that's what faith is.\n\nA light that remains on, even when we cannot see the road.","category":"Hope & Encouragement","images":[],"publicContacts":{"name":"","email":"","phone":"","link":""},"videos":[],"eventDate":"2026-11-05","eventLocation":"","sourceLinks":[],"publishedAt":"2026-11-05","featured":true,"updatedAt":"2026-11-05T22:27:59.920Z","status":"published","feedStart":"2026-11-05","feedEnd":"","featuredRoom":false}],"rates":[{"hash":"6e44a19c9e9e505d77d357ecdd924026980bcdc79a1a345f47d59725146ad46b","time":1793917110900},{"hash":"6e44a19c9e9e505d77d357ecdd924026980bcdc79a1a345f47d59725146ad46b","time":1793917269835},{"hash":"6e44a19c9e9e505d77d357ecdd924026980bc